## Build the backend

The first build takes two passes, and `first-build.sh` runs them:

```bash
{{#e2e}}cd backend
{{/e2e}}sh first-build.sh
```

It runs `mvn -Dexeris.codegen.skip=true compile`, then `mvn verify`. The annotation processor writes
the entity metadata to `target/classes/exeris-metadata` during `compile`, and `compile` runs after
`exeris:generate`. So the first pass writes the metadata with generation skipped, and the second
generates the code and its tests from that metadata, compiles them and runs the tests. Do not run
`mvn clean` between the passes: it deletes the metadata the first pass wrote.

Once `src/main/generated/java` exists, a build is one pass, `mvn verify`. Commit the generated tree
once your own code depends on a generated type: a build from an empty tree compiles your code before
anything is generated.
